Gateway:
- have a web3 library to access the BLOOM FILTER in the blockchain
- have a post method which allows user to request access (Authorization) -- return back access granted/denied
|-> user will provide USER_ID, methods, and resource as parameters. timestamp will be generated by the server
- have access to the latest transaction in the blockchain ledger containing the bloom filter
- have the bloom filter hash methods to acquire the bloom filter result
- access granted will called the "update" method from the smart contract

- initialize bloom filter with some existing data as start and update the blockchain


User:
- have a post request method in getting access to the gateway (providing the parameters)
- received either access granted/denied

Blockchain:
- have an event regarding bloom filter
- have an update method where update the bloom filter to the latest one.